From: Brady <brady@aioscilloscope.com>
Subject: drm/bridge: dw-hdmi: the HPD work tolerates a CEC adapter not yet set (6.12)
Copyright (C) 2026 Olympian LED, Inc.

The BSP's DesignWare HDMI hot-plug work notified the CEC adapter without
checking that one had been registered, so a monitor plugged in before the
CEC device probed caused a NULL-pointer oops. Skip the CEC notification
until the adapter exists.

---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-hdmi.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-hdmi.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-hdmi.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-hdmi.c
@@ -642,7 +642,7 @@
 			if (hdmi->plat_data->set_ddc_io)
 				hdmi->plat_data->set_ddc_io(data, hdmi->hpd_state);
 #if IS_REACHABLE(CONFIG_DRM_DW_HDMI_CEC)
-			if (hdmi->cec_adap->devnode.registered)
+			if (hdmi->cec_adap && hdmi->cec_adap->devnode.registered)
 				cec_queue_pin_hpd_event(hdmi->cec_adap,
 							hdmi->hpd_state,
 							ktime_get());
